- six authority/registration drifts;
- active-orbit, probability-transport, cubic-germ, and inactive-neutrality
  corruption;
- reciprocal-direction, endpoint-exhaustion, witness, and odds-inversion
  errors;
- compatibility rank, active weight-class, and varying-extension overclaims;
- static, ordered, hidden-state, axiom, gravity, obligation, TOE, and retained
  overclaims.

The independent runner rejects 27 faults through a separately organized
Boolean-coefficient proof.  It adds independent H1 runner/cache pin mutations,
direction omission, Möbius-uniqueness, nonlinear-interaction, opposite-slope,
active-class, and constant-only failures.

Every mutation must fail at least one top-level check.  A survivor blocks
cache generation and packaging.
